  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0069_81642c7f540f.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 431px;\" /></p><p>Magnitude of magnetic field due to semi-infinite portion of wire AB at point C&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Magnitude of magnetic field due to semicircular arc BD at point C&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Magnitude of magnetic field due to semi-infinite portion&nbsp;DE&nbsp;at point C&nbsp;is&nbsp;0.</p><p>Using right-hand rule, it can be seen that directions of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;both outwards from the plane.</p><p>Therefore, the magnitude of net magnetic field at point C is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"
  }
}